  "place_labels": "Town names on the anchors are orientation, not measurement points. Every discharge figure is read at a model cell, and where label_is_orientation_only is true that cell is more than 5 km from the town. In terrain this steep a main stem and a creek sit in adjacent cells, so a label placed on the wrong reach is the easiest error to make on this figure.",
  "shape_vs_rank": "Ranking a window mean against the same window in prior years answers 'was this reach high for the date'. It does not answer 'did a flood wave pass'. Those come apart here: every anchor below ranks first or near it, and only some have a hydrograph shaped like a flood. Read rise_factor and hydrograph_shape before describing any reach as flooding.",
  "reading": "Rain peaks first, rivers peak after. The gap between a catchment's rain day and its river's peak day is the response time, and it is longer for reaches further down."
